    "The MMLU benchmark stands for 'Massive Multitask Language Understanding.'",
    "MMLU is a significant evaluation tool used to assess the knowledge capabilities of large language models (LLMs).",
    "MMLU was launched in September 2020.",
    "MMLU consists of a dataset that includes around 14,000 multiple-choice questions covering 57 different subjects.",
    "The subjects in MMLU range widely, encompassing areas such as science, history, law, and medicine.",
    "The primary purpose of MMLU is to measure the breadth of knowledge that an LLM possesses.",
    "MMLU evaluates how much general knowledge the model has rather than how deeply it understands specific topics.",
    "The questions in the MMLU dataset are sourced from real exams, such as the USMLE and the USGRE, as well as other educational materials.",
    "Researchers use MMLU to test an LLM by sending the model 14,000 questions and calculating how many it answers correctly.",
    "The accuracy score derived from testing with MMLU provides insight into the model's knowledge level.",
    "A notable challenge with MMLU is that the questions are publicly available, which can lead to 'contamination' in future LLMs.",
    "Contamination occurs when newer models perform better simply because they have seen the questions before.",
    "MMLU has been a foundational benchmark in the field of LLM evaluation."
] 

